  "document": {
    "title": "File creation ownership in iiCalendar",
    "role": "guide",
    "authority": "markdown_source"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# File creation ownership in iiCalendar\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "File creation ownership in iiCalendar"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "Calendar index databases and connection documents are opened by the separate\n`examples/file-provider` application adapter using the native provider. Calendar\nschema, queries, transactions, recurrence and calendar semantics stay in\niiCalendar, which has no provider SDK dependency.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "The common [ownership contract](../../iiFileProvider/docs/FILE_OWNERSHIP.md) defines stream, staging, control-file and\ninstalled-package rules. Source regression tests remain with this module; the\nworkspace creation audit also checks these boundaries. Build/deployment and target\nruntime validation are separate evidence.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 12,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 17,
      "raw": "The application passes an already-open SQLite connection to `Store` and keeps\nexclusive use of it for the store lifetime. Account documents use the calendar\nmodule's metadata-only document API and provider-owned file publication.\nExisting applications using `Store(path)` or the removed account file methods\nmust migrate to this adapter and rebuild.\n"
    }
  ],
